course: dictionary
lesson: 699
title: Banter or bullying?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Banter means friendly, playful teasing and joking talk between people. Friends who are relaxed together often have banter. The word can also be a verb, so you might say friends banter with each other.
explain: The clues in the words around banter tell you if it is fun or hurtful. «It's not banter if only one side is laughing.» Ask yourself who is laughing. If the person being teased is laughing too, it is banter. If they look upset, it is not banter.
explain: Be careful with the words "it's just banter". «It's just banter, innit,» he says afterwards. Saying it is just banter does not make a hurtful joke okay. Check how the other person feels, not how the joker feels.
fact: Banter means friendly, playful teasing and joking talk.
fact: Banter can be a noun or a verb: friends banter with each other.
fact: «Teasing is only banter if everyone, including the person teased, is laughing.»
fact: If a joke keeps hurting someone, or is about how they look, it can be bullying, and a teacher should be told.
fact: «Banter» is British for jokey teasing, and «bants» is slang for jokes that are meant to be funny, though sometimes they hurt.
exercise: «Teasing is only banter if everyone, including the person teased, is laughing.» What does this tell you about banter? | *Everyone is laughing, including the person teased | Nobody is allowed to tease | Teasing is always rude | Only one person is laughing
exercise: Ravi's friends keep making jokes about his glasses, and Ravi looks sad. Is this banter? | *No, it hurts him and it is about how he looks | Yes, because they say it is just banter | Yes, because friends always do this | Only if Ravi makes the jokes himself
exercise: What does banter mean? | A type of sweet | A serious argument | *Friendly, playful teasing and joking talk | Quiet reading time
test: «It's not banter if only one side is laughing.» What is the clue in this sentence? | *Who is laughing | The colour of the page | Whether it is written down | The number of words
test: Banter can be a verb. Which word shows the past tense? | banter | bantering | *bantered | banters
exam: If a joke keeps hurting someone, what is the right thing to do? | Keep joking so they get used to it | *Tell a teacher | Say it is just banter and walk away | Laugh along so nobody notices
